    "why_this_is_published": "The era boundary falls INSIDE any season-scale cohort, and \u00a72's gate is pooled over the held-out range so it cannot see the split's era composition. ADR-007 records the regimes differing at 1.596 unresolved doubtful per date short-lead against 0.917 legacy; unresolved rows are excluded, so the exclusion rate is era-dependent and concentrated on the scarcest status. A cohort can therefore clear the floor BECAUSE of the era it is evaluated in while being fitted substantially on the other one. These are denominators, so publishing them costs no unblind."
